# Phase 2 CLI acceptance — six-family corpus-integrity surface (D-10/D-11)

`QAI_DATA_DIR` points the real `qai` binary at a fresh temp database (set by the
harness); each `console` block runs in order against that one database, so
`db migrate` must come first and `test-edition-min@0.1.0` is activated before
any verify.

A reference-less import records the QV-015 skip: `reference_comparison` must
report `skipped`, never `pass`, and the overall exit stays 0.

```console
$ qai db migrate
migrations applied; schema version 21

```

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-min/manifest.json
imported test-edition-min@0.1.0 to Staged
note: synthetic test data — non-canonical (ADR-0101 fallback)

```

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-min@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-min@0.1.0 (generation 1)

```

The human surface names all six families and the exit gate.

```console
$ qai quran verify
QURAN VERIFY
counts: pass — 2 checks pass
addressing: pass — 4 checks pass
unicode: pass — 1 checks pass
checksums: pass — 3 checks pass
roundtrip: pass — 1 checks pass
reference_comparison: skipped — reference comparison skipped: no reference corpus configured (ADR-0114; OD-03 owner gate)
exit: 0

```

```console
$ qai quran verify --json
{
  "addressing": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.edition_active",
      "quran.ayah_identifiers",
      "quran.division_coverage",
      "quran.basmala_policy"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "4 checks pass"
  },
  "checksums": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.edition_checksum",
      "quran.structure_hash",
      "quran.token_order_hash"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "3 checks pass"
  },
  "counts": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.surah_count",
      "quran.ayah_count"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "2 checks pass"
  },
  "reference_comparison": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.reference_corpus"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "reason": "not evaluated; skipped is never counted as pass (D-10)",
    "status": "skipped",
    "summary": "reference comparison skipped: no reference corpus configured (ADR-0114; OD-03 owner gate)"
  },
  "roundtrip": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.token_roundtrip"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "1 checks pass"
  },
  "unicode": {
    "checks": [
      "quran.unicode_form"
    ],
    "gate": "exit::OK",
    "status": "pass",
    "summary": "1 checks pass"
  }
}

```

`--deep` upgrades the sampled round-trip to a full-corpus scan; the family
classification is otherwise identical.

```console
$ qai quran verify --deep
QURAN VERIFY
counts: pass — 2 checks pass
addressing: pass — 4 checks pass
unicode: pass — 1 checks pass
checksums: pass — 3 checks pass
roundtrip: pass — 1 checks pass
reference_comparison: skipped — reference comparison skipped: no reference corpus configured (ADR-0114; OD-03 owner gate)
exit: 0

```
